<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2064] Correct p2p deployment logic/tests for binary marshaller</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2064</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In current implementation p2p deployment is disabled for cache when binary marshaller is used. It pursues an ability to use peer-deployed compute tasks and not to clear cache when deployment owner leaves the grid.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thus, existing tests should be disabled/corrected for the binary marshaller and new tests that use BinaryObject API should be added.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, there are TODOs in the code related to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1272&quot; title=&quot;PortableMarshaller: issues when different class loaders are used&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-1272&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-1272&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ticket, which has been closed. Need to revisit and fix those todos, if needed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
